docs-preview-bot: Link check passed, but one broken link found in /guides/streaming.md referencing an old example path — I updated it in the PR.

Carla (Docs): Great. Can someone volunteer to run a quick read-through for wording? I can handle the streaming page if nobody else is free.

Ben T.: I can take the SDK Python page tonight.

Evelyn (SDK): I'll review the TS and Go snippets tomorrow morning. Also will run the snippet examples through a small smoke test to validate runtime semantics.

Alice M.: Thanks team — aiming to merge tomorrow after the reviews. Tag me on comments for any follow-ups. :thumbsup:

Ben T.: Quick follow-up Q — do we want to mention `max_retries` builtin parameter in SDKs or just show helper? Some SDKs have opt-in retry config.

Evelyn (SDK): Good point. I'll add a short note: "Where SDKs expose `max_retries`, prefer that for idempotent calls; otherwise use a helper for non-idempotent flows."

Alice M.: Perfect. Closing loop — will push final edits in an hour. Thanks all!
